==> Error: `spack unload` requires Spack's shell support.
  
  To set up shell support, run the command below for your shell.
  
  For bash/zsh/sh:
    . /gpfs/packages/spack/spack-rhel8/share/spack/setup-env.sh
  
  For csh/tcsh:
    source /gpfs/packages/spack/spack-rhel8/share/spack/setup-env.csh
  
  For fish:
    source /gpfs/packages/spack/spack-rhel8/share/spack/setup-env.fish
  
  For Windows batch:
    source /gpfs/packages/spack/spack-rhel8/share/spack/spack_cmd.bat
  
  Or, if you do not want to use shell support, run one of these instead:
  
      eval `spack unload --sh  ` /i3vva2q  # bash/zsh/sh
      eval `spack unload --csh ` /i3vva2q  # csh/tcsh
      eval `spack unload --fish` /i3vva2q  # fish
      eval `spack unload --bat ` /i3vva2q  # batch
  
  If you have already set up Spack's shell support but still receive
  this message, please make sure to call Spack via the `spack` command
  without any path components (such as `bin/spack`).
  
